# Wave W17-AA (Route 222): solar sand — the straight beach road’s pale sand, design-authorised: a warm sun-bleached sand running straight from Lake Gallant’s shore to Brightshore’s gate, carrying rare white-gold glints in its tread — the panels’ light arriving before the panels do (design: the road runs straight and bright all the way). Split from Route 213’s salt sand behind it by warmth entire (sun-bleached vs salt-pale) and from Route 221’s coast sand by purpose: this sand commutes, that sand wanders between tide pools.
